From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris McLaughlin <19711592+qBitnaut@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 19:08:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] SL7 local: arm64: dts: qcom: x1e80100-romulus: Light
 the camera indicator for both cameras

The white camera indicator (GPIO 225) was only a panic indicator for lack
of a "camera on" trigger. The V4L2 core has one: a sensor with a "privacy"
LED reference turns that LED on while it streams.

Label the LED camera_privacy_led, drop panic-indicator, and reference it
as "privacy" from the front RGB OV02C10 and, on the 13.8 inch model, the
IR VD55G0 (which needs the previous patch to look it up). Windows lights
the LED for the front RGB camera only (ACPI CAMP owns GPIO 225, CAMI has
none); lighting it for the IR camera too is deliberate, so that a face
scan is visible.

Both sensors share the one LED. led_get() allows several consumers and
the sysfs-disable flag is not counted, but the core keeps no reference
count either: if one camera stops while the other still streams, the LED
goes off. Both cameras streaming at the same time is rare enough to leave
as is.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate (SL7 specific)
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi | 15 ++++++++++++---
 .../dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13.dts     |  7 ++++++-
 2 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi
index 12827c0bffec..8f0448d42b0c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi
@@ -94,15 +94,21 @@ leds {
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
 		pinctrl-0 = <&cam_indicator_en>;

-		led-camera-indicator {
+		/*
+		 * The camera indicator. Both cameras reference it as their
+		 * "privacy" LED, so the V4L2 core lights it while either one
+		 * streams. Windows lights it for the front RGB camera only
+		 * (ACPI CAMP, GPIO 225); the IR camera lights it here by
+		 * choice. The core has no reference count: when one camera
+		 * stops while the other still streams, the LED goes off.
+		 */
+		camera_privacy_led: led-camera-indicator {
 			label = "white:camera-indicator";
 			function = LED_FUNCTION_INDICATOR;
 			color = <LED_COLOR_ID_WHITE>;
 			gpios = <&tlmm 225 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 			linux,default-trigger = "none";
 			default-state = "off";
-			/* Reuse as a panic indicator until we get a "camera on" trigger */
-			panic-indicator;
 		};
 	};

@@ -959,6 +965,9 @@ camera@36 {

 		orientation = <0>; /* front facing */

+		leds = <&camera_privacy_led>;
+		led-names = "privacy";
+
 		avdd-supply = <&vreg_l5m_2p8>;
 		dvdd-supply = <&vreg_l1m_1p2>;
 		dovdd-supply = <&vreg_l3m_1p8>;
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13.dts
index 0ff200622136..c048795edd00 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13.dts
@@ -89,7 +89,8 @@ &cci0_i2c0 {
 	 * "linux-sl7 (IR test)" boot entry alone (patch "vd55g: illuminator").
 	 * On every other boot the property is ignored: no GPIO is a strobe output
 	 * and there is no led_mode control. There is no `leds = <...>` link to a
-	 * flash LED and no led-names: the driver never drives the PMIC.
+	 * flash LED: the driver never drives the PMIC. The only `leds` link is the
+	 * "privacy" camera indicator below.
 	 *
 	 * The illuminator is the PM8550 flash (QCOM0C27, 700 mA), probably
 	 * channels 1 and 4 together. The ganged test LED under &pm8550_flash
@@ -120,6 +121,10 @@ camera@10 {

 		orientation = <0>; /* front facing */

+		/* The camera indicator lights while this sensor streams */
+		leds = <&camera_privacy_led>;
+		led-names = "privacy";
+
 		/* GPIO 1 is the strobe output; ignored unless vd55g.illuminator=1 */
 		st,leds = <1>;

